// Normalizes the names of recurring numbered competitions (issues #270, #285)
// and classifies every known competition instance into its curated
// competition group (issue #445).
//
// BBL and TP named the same recurring competition tracks inconsistently over
// the years: the top-tier season track ran uninterrupted as 1..29 but was
// called "Season N" (1-18, before "Minor Season" existed so the top tier
// needed no "Major" qualifier), then "Major Season N" (19-24), then
// "tLoEGBBL Säsong N" (26-29, Swedish for "season" -- Minor Season was
// discontinued after 25 and the source system simply switched language, not
// competition concept). Ogretoberfest, Chaos Cup, Moot Mania and Dungeon Bowl
// picked up stray prefixes/spacing along the way, and each of the first three
// tracks' very first instalment was never numbered at all ("Chaos Cup" rather
// than "Chaos Cup 1"). BBL's three Reserves Rumble events (bblIds 7, 16, 23)
// were never numbered either -- they all carry the identical raw name.
// All of them are renamed here to the canonical form.
//
// This file now serves two purposes: renaming (entries that carry a `name`)
// and group classification (every entry, via `competitionGroup`). The 50
// entries added for classification only carry `externalIds` and
// `competitionGroup` -- deliberately no `name` -- so they cannot rename a
// scraped competition by accident; an omitted field is left exactly as the
// BBL/TP importers set it (see the overlay note below). `competitionGroup`
// values are plain strings here, but each processor turns its string into the
// group's `Name`-system external ref (via ReferenceResolverService's
// `competitionGroupRef`) and resolves it against this run's own
// ExternalIdMap -- the same mechanism every other reference in this file
// uses. That is why competition-groups.json5 and leagues.json5 in this
// directory are symlinks to the before-other-importers originals: this phase
// re-processes the same curated catalog to populate its own map with those
// groups' ids, even though the group catalog itself is curated in the
// before-other-importers phase, not in this file.
//
// Runs AFTER the BBL/TP importers (this is the after-other-importers
// directory): each entry matches its existing database row by that row's own
// source-system id alone. Competitions carry NO "Name" external id (issue
// #285 removed it: a shared Name id made distinct same-named competitions --
// exactly the Reserves Rumble case -- dedupe onto a single row via
// resolveExistingByExternalIds), so supplying one here would be a dead lookup
// key.
//
// Each rename entry is the new name plus the external ids that match the
// existing row. Competitions upsert as overlays (issue #174), so a field
// this file omits -- era, type -- is left exactly as the BBL/TP importers set
// it. That is why there are no eras, league or rules sets declared here: with
// nothing to reference, there is nothing to redeclare.
//
// Not renamed (already consistent, or out of scope per issue #270/#285):
// Korpen 1-9, Moot Mania 2-4, NAA/NAA 2, Ogretoberfest 2-9/11/13, Chaos Cup
// 2-7, Minor Season 18/19/21-23/25, Dungeon Bowl 1, Major Season 19-24,
// Stunty Leeg 1/2, the one-off cups (Blitzmania!, Champions of..., Fright
// Night, Snöbollskrieg) and GBBL 1. type is deliberately not supplied: BBL/TP
// already classify every row correctly, and an omitted field is left
// untouched.
//
// Source-data facts worth recording here: BBL's `s` id sequence has no s=9
// at all (not a gap in this file -- it never existed on the source site), and
// s=5 (Snöbollskrieg) exists and is named on BBL but has no cached subpage in
// the mirror this data was curated from.
{
  externalSystems: [
    { name: 'tloeg.bbleague.se', category: 'imported_data_source' },
    { name: 'tourplay.net', category: 'imported_data_source' },
  ],

  competitions: [
    // -- The Major Season track, seasons 1-18 (BBL, First era). Named plain
    // "Season N" back when there was no Minor Season to distinguish from.
    // The numeric id is the competition's BBL `s` value from the p=se
    // competition list -- the only key competitions are matched by.
    {
      name: 'Major Season 1',
      externalIds: [{ system: 'tloeg.bbleague.se', id: '1' }],
      competitionGroup: 'Major Season',
    },
